Aim: To create and execute an Ansible playbook that installs Apache and deploys a simple HTML web application.
Steps to perform
1. Open Ubuntu terminal.
2. Check whether Ansible is installed:
   ansible --version
3. Set the UTF-8 locale:
   export LANG=C.UTF-8
   export LC_ALL=C.UTF-8
4. Create a project directory:
   mkdir -p ~/ansible-webapp
   cd ~/ansible-webapp
5. Create the playbook file:
   nano webapp.yml
6. Enter the YAML playbook from your manual. It contains five tasks:
   - Install Apache using ansible.builtin.apt.
   - Start and enable Apache using ansible.builtin.service.
   - Create /var/www/html/index.html using ansible.builtin.copy.
   - Verify the website using ansible.builtin.uri.
   - Display a success message using ansible.builtin.debug.
7. Save the file using Ctrl + O → Enter → Ctrl + X.
8. Execute the playbook:
   ansible-playbook webapp.yml --ask-become-pass
9. Enter your Ubuntu password when requested.
10. Install curl:
sudo apt update
sudo apt install curl -y


11. Check Apache's status:
sudo systemctl status apache2


12. Test the website:
curl http://localhost


13. Open Chrome or Firefox and visit:
http://localhost


14. Verify that the web page displays:
Hello from Ansible!
My web application was deployed automatically.
